<title>FRANCE: French budget breakdown at end August.</title>
<headline>French budget breakdown at end August.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cumulative net tax receipts stood at 864.9 billion francs at the end of August, up 5.4 percent from the same period a year earlier, the finance ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>General cumulative budget revenues were up 4.5 percent at 817.3 billion francs.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in spending was 3.2 percent. The central government budget deficit totalled 334.2 billion francs.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1996 year forecast):</p>
<p> BALANCE			  end Aug 96 end Aug 95  pct</p>
<p> Total budget spending	  1,061.4  1,028.6     3.2</p>
<p> Total receipts		     817.3    782.4     4.5</p>
<p> General budget deficit	  -244.1   -246.2</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts	-90.1    -89.4</p>
<p> TOTAL CENTRAL GOVT DEFICIT    -334.2   -335.6</p>
<p>				     end Aug 96   Aug 95  pct	1996</p>
<p> REVENUES							   budget law</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		    864.9    820.3   5.4    1,401.1</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p> -- income tax			 196.4    189.1   3.9	310.1</p>
<p> -- net company tax		   77.6     65.2  19.0	131.6</p>
<p> -- petrol duties		     96.0     92.3   4.0	148.5</p>
<p> -- net Value Added Tax	    397.8    368.2   8.0	634.7</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		    97.1    105.5  -8.0	176.2</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		     75.2     77.6  -3.1	132.4</p>
<p> Local authority and EU charges -168.0   -155.8   7.8     -252.5</p>
<p> General budget receipts	   772.1    742.1   4.0    1,281.0</p>
<p>				   end Aug 96   Aug 95   pct</p>
<p>SPENDING</p>
<p> Ordinary civil spending	  866.4    841.9   2.9</p>
<p> of which debt			145.9    143.9   1.4</p>
<p> Capital civil spending	    64.4     60.7   6.1</p>
<p> Ordinary military spending	75.4     72.5   4.0</p>
<p> Capital military spending	 55.2     53.5   3.2</p>
<p> TOTAL BUDGET SPENDING	  1,061.4  1,028.6   3.2</p>
